      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given:\n- The geometric mean (GM) of two positive real numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is \\(\\sqrt{3}\\).\n- The harmonic mean (HM) of the same numbers is \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\).\n\nWe are to find these two numbers.\n\n**Step 1: Recall the definitions of geometric mean and harmonic mean.**\n\nThe geometric mean of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\nSquaring both sides, we get:\n\\[\nab = 3\n\\]\n\nThe harmonic mean of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is given by:\n\\[\nHM = \\frac{2ab}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Substitute \\(ab = 3\\) into the harmonic mean formula.**\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2ab}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(ab = 3\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{2 \\cdot 3}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Solve for \\(a + b\\).**\n\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nCross-multiplying gives:\n\\[\n6 \\cdot 2 = 3 \\cdot (a + b)\n\\]\n\\[\n12 = 3(a + b)\n\\]\n\\[\na + b = 4\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Solve the system of equations.**\n\nWe already know:\n\\[\nab = 3\n\\]\n\\[\na + b = 4\n\\]\n\nThese equations represent a quadratic equation whose roots are \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). The quadratic equation can be written as:\n\\[\nt^2 - (a + b)t + ab = 0\n\\]\nSubstituting the known values:\n\\[\nt^2 - 4t + 3 = 0\n\\]\n\n**Step 5: Solve the quadratic equation.**\n\n\\[\nt^2 - 4t + 3 = 0\n\\]\nFactoring the quadratic equation:\n\\[\n(t - 1)(t - 3) = 0\n\\]\nThus, the solutions are:\n\\[\nt = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad t = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the two numbers are \\(1\\) and \\(3\\).\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{1, 3}\n\\]",
